WEBVTT

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:09.577
The Call of the Wild by Jack London Retold by Gina D.B.

00:00:09.617 --> 00:00:24.456
Clement Copyright Black Cat Publishing, 2002 Chapter 1 The Southland Buck did not read the newspapers.

00:00:24.516 --> 00:00:29.740
He did not know that there was trouble for every big strong dog in California.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.254
Men found a yellow metal called gold in the Klondike.

00:00:34.314 --> 00:00:38.951
They needed big strong dogs with furry coats to work in the north.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.585
Buck lived in a big house in the sunny Santa Clara Valley.

00:00:42.645 --> 00:00:45.548
The house was called Judge Miller's Place.

00:00:45.608 --> 00:00:50.094
Around the house, there were big gardens, fruit trees and horses.

00:00:50.154 --> 00:00:54.358
Buck was born here, and now he was four years old.

00:00:54.418 --> 00:00:58.060
There were other dogs, too, but they were not important.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.852
Buck was the king.

00:00:59.912 --> 00:01:01.903
Judge Miller's place was his.

00:01:01.963 --> 00:01:04.625
He swam and hunted with the judge's sons.

00:01:04.685 --> 00:01:06.946
He walked with the judge's daughters.

00:01:07.006 --> 00:01:11.100
He carried the judge's grandsons on his back and played with them.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:15.512
In the winter, Buck sat at the judge's feet in front of the fire.

00:01:15.572 --> 00:01:21.295
Buck's father was a big Saint Bernard, and his mother was a Scottish sheepdog.

00:01:21.355 --> 00:01:27.068
Buck weighed 140 pounds, and he was a happy and handsome dog.

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:33.230
In the fall of 1897, men from all over the world went to the Klondike.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:38.392
They wanted to find gold, but Buck did not read the newspapers.

00:01:38.452 --> 00:01:43.224
Manuel was the gardener's helper and he needed money for his big family.

00:01:43.284 --> 00:01:47.937
One evening the judge was out of the house and Manuel and Buck went for a walk.

00:01:47.997 --> 00:01:52.850
No one saw them leave and only one man saw them at the railway station.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:56.652
The man talked to Manuel and gave him some money.

00:01:56.712 --> 00:01:59.752
Then Manuel tied a rope around Buck's neck.

00:01:59.812 --> 00:02:03.983
Buck let Manuel put the rope around his neck because he was his friend.

00:02:04.043 --> 00:02:07.964
But when the other man pulled the rope, Buck could not breathe.

00:02:08.024 --> 00:02:09.765
He was angry.

00:02:09.825 --> 00:02:11.976
And he jumped at the man.

00:02:12.036 --> 00:02:14.727
The man caught him and suddenly Buck was on his back.

00:02:14.787 --> 00:02:18.128
His tongue was out of his mouth and he was unable to move.

00:02:18.188 --> 00:02:21.969
In the past, no one ever did this to him.

00:02:22.029 --> 00:02:25.858
The two men put him on the train in the baggage car.

00:02:25.918 --> 00:02:29.326
When Buck woke up, the train was moving.

00:02:29.385 --> 00:02:31.156
He was angry.

00:02:31.216 --> 00:02:34.476
The man watched him, but Buck was too quick.

00:02:34.536 --> 00:02:37.167
He bit the man's hand.

00:02:37.227 --> 00:02:43.868
That evening, the man took Buck to the back room of a saloon in San Francisco.

00:02:43.928 --> 00:02:46.599
The saloonkeeper looked at his hand.

00:02:46.659 --> 00:02:48.719
I only got $50 for it.

00:02:48.779 --> 00:02:49.989
The man said.

00:02:50.049 --> 00:02:51.790
How much did the other man get?

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.422
The saloonkeeper asked.

00:02:53.481 --> 00:02:54.934
$100.

00:02:54.993 --> 00:02:56.264
That makes $150.

00:02:56.324 --> 00:02:58.975
That's a good price for a dog like him.

00:02:59.035 --> 00:03:01.806
Come on, help me put him into the crate."

00:03:01.866 --> 00:03:07.829
Buck tried to attack the two men, but they pulled the rope again and again.

00:03:07.889 --> 00:03:09.980
Buck suffered terribly.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.562
His neck, throat, and tongue hurt a lot.

00:03:13.622 --> 00:03:17.582
The men took off the rope and threw him into a crate.

00:03:17.642 --> 00:03:21.303
Buck spent the night in the back room of the saloon.

00:03:21.363 --> 00:03:23.373
He was very angry.

00:03:23.433 --> 00:03:26.064
He could not understand why he was there.

00:03:26.124 --> 00:03:28.414
What did these strange men want?

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.815
Why was he a prisoner in a crate?

00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:32.885
Where was the judge?

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:38.306
The next morning, four men took the crate to the railway station.

00:03:38.366 --> 00:03:42.234
They put it on a train that was going to the north.

00:03:42.294 --> 00:03:48.236
For two days and two nights, Buck did not eat or drink.

00:03:48.296 --> 00:03:50.998
He was confused and angry.

00:03:51.058 --> 00:03:53.291
Men on the train laughed at him.

00:03:53.351 --> 00:03:55.392
He threw himself against the crate.

00:03:55.452 --> 00:03:58.956
He growled and barked at the men.

00:03:59.016 --> 00:04:03.910
Buck was very thirsty, but he had no water.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.242
His tongue and throat were very dry.

00:04:07.302 --> 00:04:11.308
His eyes were red and his anger grew.

00:04:11.368 --> 00:04:13.792
He was glad for one thing.

00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:16.134
The rope was off his neck.

00:04:16.193 --> 00:04:21.737
He did not want another rope around his neck.

00:04:21.796 --> 00:04:25.599
Exercise five.

00:04:25.659 --> 00:04:27.470
Did you know?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:28.351
One.

00:04:28.371 --> 00:04:30.082
Two.

00:04:30.141 --> 00:04:37.482
Three.

00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:51.836
Chapter 2 The Northland In Seattle, four men carried the crate to a garden with a high wall.

00:04:51.896 --> 00:04:54.948
A fat man with a red sweater looked at him.

00:04:55.008 --> 00:04:59.112
Bucked through himself against the crate, he growled and barked.

00:04:59.172 --> 00:05:01.824
The man brought a hatchet and a clove.

00:05:01.884 --> 00:05:03.454
Are you going to take him out now?

00:05:03.514 --> 00:05:04.836
Asked one of the men.

00:05:04.895 --> 00:05:07.037
Sure, the man said.

00:05:07.097 --> 00:05:10.282
He hit the crate with a hatchet to open it.

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:12.806
The four men ran away.

00:05:12.866 --> 00:05:16.328
They went to sit on the high wall to watch the show.

00:05:16.388 --> 00:05:19.350
Buck threw himself against the wood of the crate.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.551
He bit it and growled.

00:05:21.611 --> 00:05:23.422
He wanted to get out.

00:05:23.482 --> 00:05:26.264
The man with the hatchet opened the crate.

00:05:26.324 --> 00:05:29.886
Then he put down the hatchet and took the club.

00:05:29.946 --> 00:05:32.858
Buck was really a red-eyed devil.

00:05:32.918 --> 00:05:37.034
His hair stood up and his eyes were red with anger.

00:05:37.094 --> 00:05:41.429
He jumped straight at the man and his mouth was ready to bite.

00:05:41.489 --> 00:05:45.360
At that moment the man hit him with the club.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:48.762
He fell to the ground on his back.

00:05:48.822 --> 00:05:52.734
This was the first time he was hit with a club.

00:05:52.794 --> 00:05:54.875
He did not understand.

00:05:54.935 --> 00:06:00.932
He jumped at the man again and again the man hit him with the club.

00:06:00.992 --> 00:06:03.436
He fell to the ground again.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:09.878
This time Buck knew that it was the club, but his anger was so great that he did not stop.

00:06:09.938 --> 00:06:15.530
He jumped at the man a dozen times, and a dozen times the club hit him.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:19.412
There was blood on his nose, mouth and ears.

00:06:19.472 --> 00:06:22.573
Then the man hit him very hard on the nose.

00:06:22.633 --> 00:06:24.413
The pain was terrible.

00:06:24.473 --> 00:06:26.110
It was agony.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:30.728
Buck jumped at the man again, and the man threw him to the ground.

00:06:30.788 --> 00:06:34.260
Buck did not move for some time.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:38.752
He knows how to teach a dog a lesson, said one of the four men.

00:06:38.812 --> 00:06:41.734
Then they returned to the train station.

00:06:41.794 --> 00:06:44.956
Buck slowly opened his eyes.

00:06:45.016 --> 00:06:47.087
He could not move.

00:06:47.147 --> 00:06:50.238
He watched the man in the red sweater.

00:06:50.298 --> 00:06:56.002
The fat man was reading the saloon keeper's letter and said, Your name is Buck.

00:06:56.062 --> 00:07:01.004
Well, Buck, he said in a friendly voice, Now you know your place.

00:07:01.064 --> 00:07:03.775
Be a good dog and we'll be friends.

00:07:03.835 --> 00:07:07.548
Be a bad dog, and I must use my club again.

00:07:07.608 --> 00:07:09.068
Understand?

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:12.590
As he spoke, he touched Buck's head.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:17.603
Buck was angry inside, but he did not move.

00:07:17.663 --> 00:07:22.902
When the man brought him water and meat, Buck drank and ate.

00:07:22.962 --> 00:07:26.341
He learned that a man with a club was stronger than him.

00:07:26.361 --> 00:07:28.792
He never forgot it.

00:07:28.852 --> 00:07:31.786
Life was now fiercer.

00:07:31.846 --> 00:07:35.028
Each day, other dogs came.

00:07:35.088 --> 00:07:38.411
The man in the red sweater hit many dogs.

00:07:38.471 --> 00:07:42.834
Buck understood that a dog must obey a man with a club.

00:07:42.894 --> 00:07:44.737
He was a master.

00:07:44.796 --> 00:07:49.593
One dog did not obey, and he was killed.

00:07:49.652 --> 00:07:54.006
Men often came to talk to the man in the red sweater.

00:07:54.066 --> 00:07:58.488
When they paid money, the men took one or more of the dogs.

00:07:58.548 --> 00:08:01.619
Those dogs never came back.

00:08:01.679 --> 00:08:03.220
Where did they go?

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.440
Buck thought.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.120
He was afraid of the future.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:11.412
One day, a short man came to look at Buck.

00:08:11.472 --> 00:08:13.703
The man spoke bad English.

00:08:13.763 --> 00:08:15.294
That's a strong dog.

00:08:15.354 --> 00:08:16.784
How much?

00:08:16.844 --> 00:08:17.584
$300.

00:08:17.644 --> 00:08:19.318
Said the man in the red sweater.

00:08:19.378 --> 00:08:21.253
And it's a gift at that price.

00:08:21.313 --> 00:08:23.064
Perot smiled.

00:08:23.124 --> 00:08:26.016
The price of dogs was high at that time.

00:08:26.076 --> 00:08:31.050
Perot knew dogs, and he knew Buck was an excellent dog.

00:08:31.109 --> 00:08:34.441
Buck saw money passed between the two men.

00:08:34.501 --> 00:08:41.816
He was not surprised when he and a Newfoundland dog called Curly were taken away by the small man.

00:08:41.876 --> 00:08:45.750
He took them to a ship called the Norwall.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:50.324
From the ship, he and Curly looked back at Seattle.

00:08:50.384 --> 00:08:54.676
It was the last time they saw the warm Southland.

00:08:54.736 --> 00:08:58.427
Perot took Buck and Curly to Francois.

00:08:58.487 --> 00:09:05.650
Perot was a French-Canadian, but Francois was half Indian and had very dark skin.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:09.792
Buck did not like these men, but he respected them.

00:09:09.852 --> 00:09:13.874
He learned that Perot and Francois were calm and fair.

00:09:13.934 --> 00:09:16.668
They knew everything about dogs.

00:09:16.728 --> 00:09:19.453
There were two other dogs on the ship.

00:09:19.513 --> 00:09:23.175
One was a big white dog called Spitz.

00:09:23.235 --> 00:09:27.348
He seemed friendly, but he was not honest.

00:09:27.408 --> 00:09:30.589
He smiled when he tried to take Buck's food.

00:09:30.649 --> 00:09:33.471
Francois was fast and hit Spitz.

00:09:33.531 --> 00:09:38.010
From this moment Buck began to like him.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:41.228
The other dog was called Dave.

00:09:41.288 --> 00:09:44.779
He was unfriendly and always wanted to be alone.

00:09:44.839 --> 00:09:49.670
Dave ate and slept and was interested in nothing.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.891
Day and night the ship sailed.

00:09:52.951 --> 00:09:59.334
Every day was the same, but Buck noticed that the weather was colder.

00:09:59.394 --> 00:10:04.485
Finally, one morning the Norwels engine stopped.

00:10:04.545 --> 00:10:07.760
Buck and the other dogs were excited.

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:09.756
something was happening.

00:10:09.816 --> 00:10:14.140
Francois leashed the dogs and took them outside.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:19.384
At the first step, Buck's feet went down into something white and soft.

00:10:19.444 --> 00:10:20.896
He jumped back.

00:10:20.956 --> 00:10:25.909
More of this white stuff was falling from the sky and fell on Buck.

00:10:25.969 --> 00:10:30.432
He shook himself, but more fell on him.

00:10:30.492 --> 00:10:35.829
He smelled it curiously, then tasted some on his tongue.

00:10:35.889 --> 00:10:40.585
It was like fire, and the next moment it disappeared.

00:10:40.645 --> 00:10:42.696
This confused him.

00:10:42.756 --> 00:10:46.209
He tried it again with the same result.

00:10:46.269 --> 00:10:48.921
People looked at him and laughed.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:53.154
It was his first snow.

00:10:53.214 --> 00:11:03.502
Chapter 3 The Law of Club and Fang Buck's first day at Daihe Beach was terrible.

00:11:03.562 --> 00:11:09.106
What a change from his comfortable happy life with the judge in the sunny Southland.

00:11:09.166 --> 00:11:12.149
Here, there was no peace or rest.

00:11:12.209 --> 00:11:15.151
There was only confusion and noise.

00:11:15.211 --> 00:11:21.016
There was danger everywhere, because these dogs and men were not city dogs and men.

00:11:21.076 --> 00:11:25.026
They only knew the law of club and fang.

00:11:25.086 --> 00:11:28.115
Buck never saw dogs like these.

00:11:28.175 --> 00:11:30.246
They fought like wolves.

00:11:30.306 --> 00:11:32.887
He learned this by watching Curly.

00:11:32.947 --> 00:11:35.478
She wanted to make friends with a husky.

00:11:35.538 --> 00:11:40.800
The husky jumped on Curly and he tore her face from eye to mouth.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:43.782
Wolves and huskies fight like this.

00:11:43.842 --> 00:11:46.692
They attack and then jump away.

00:11:46.752 --> 00:11:49.163
But this fight was not finished.

00:11:49.223 --> 00:11:52.966
Thirty of forty huskies came and made a circle around the fight.

00:11:53.026 --> 00:11:56.568
Curly attacked her enemy, but the husky bit her again.

00:11:56.588 --> 00:12:01.611
She fell to the ground and never stood up again.

00:12:01.671 --> 00:12:06.664
The other huskies moved in and suddenly she was under them.

00:12:06.724 --> 00:12:11.097
Buck saw Spitz run away with his red tongue out of his mouth.

00:12:11.157 --> 00:12:12.768
He was laughing.

00:12:12.828 --> 00:12:15.810
Curly was dead in the snow.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.972
Her body was almost in pieces.

00:12:19.032 --> 00:12:22.543
Buck often saw this scene in his dreams.

00:12:22.603 --> 00:12:27.434
He understood that when a dog was injured, that was the end.

00:12:27.494 --> 00:12:33.156
Spits laughed again, and from that moment Buck hated him.

00:12:33.216 --> 00:12:35.988
Soon Buck had another surprise.

00:12:36.048 --> 00:12:38.450
Francois put a harness on him.

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:42.182
Buck remembered the harnesses on horses at home.

00:12:42.242 --> 00:12:45.173
So now he must work like a horse.

00:12:45.233 --> 00:12:50.106
He must pull the sled to the forest to get firewood.

00:12:50.166 --> 00:12:55.464
He was offended, but he decided to work and do his best.

00:12:55.524 --> 00:13:00.064
He worked with Spitz and Dave and learned a lot from them.

00:13:00.124 --> 00:13:10.252
He learned to stop when Francois said, and to go when he said, those three are very good dogs.

00:13:10.312 --> 00:13:15.136
Francois told Pirot, but pulls well and learns quickly.

00:13:15.196 --> 00:13:21.612
That afternoon, Pirot bought two Huskies called Billy and Joe.

00:13:21.672 --> 00:13:23.236
They were brothers.

00:13:23.296 --> 00:13:27.567
Billy was very friendly, but Joe was the opposite.

00:13:27.627 --> 00:13:32.339
In the evening, Perot bought another dog called Solax.

00:13:32.399 --> 00:13:35.880
He was an old husky with only one eye.

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:39.982
He made no friends and wanted to be alone.

00:13:40.042 --> 00:13:44.273
That night, Buck, had another problem.

00:13:44.333 --> 00:13:46.228
Where could he sleep?

00:13:46.288 --> 00:13:49.244
Francois and Perot were in their tent.

00:13:49.304 --> 00:13:53.056
When Buck tried to enter, they shouted angrily at him.

00:13:53.116 --> 00:13:56.577
It was terribly cold and windy outside.

00:13:56.637 --> 00:14:01.188
He tried to sleep in the snow, but it was too cold.

00:14:01.248 --> 00:14:04.130
Buck walked sadly around the tent.

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:08.051
He looked for the other dogs, but he could not find them.

00:14:08.111 --> 00:14:09.782
Where were they?

00:14:09.842 --> 00:14:12.773
Buck was very cold and unhappy.

00:14:12.833 --> 00:14:15.474
He did not know what to do.

00:14:15.534 --> 00:14:18.595
Suddenly he fell into a hole.

00:14:18.655 --> 00:14:23.476
He felt something move and then heard a friendly bark.

00:14:23.536 --> 00:14:28.318
Under the snow, in the warm hole he saw Billy.

00:14:28.378 --> 00:14:33.280
Billy licked Buck's face with his warm, wet tongue.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:35.720
Another lesson.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:39.041
So that was how the dog slept.

00:14:39.101 --> 00:14:41.910
Buck chose a place and made a hole.

00:14:41.969 --> 00:14:45.218
In a minute, he was warm and asleep.

00:14:45.278 --> 00:14:49.128
He slept well, but had bad dreams.

00:14:49.188 --> 00:14:52.979
The noises of the camp woke him up the next morning.

00:14:53.039 --> 00:14:54.290
What did I say?

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:56.480
Francois shouted to Perot.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.410
That buck learns quickly.

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:00.351
Perot smiled.

00:15:00.411 --> 00:15:03.441
He was a courier for the Canadian government.

00:15:03.501 --> 00:15:08.352
He transported important documents, and he needed the best dogs.

00:15:08.412 --> 00:15:11.240
He bought three dogs that morning.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:17.800
Now there were nine dogs in a harness, and they were going up the Daihi Canyon.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:21.774
The work was hard, but Buck liked it.

00:15:21.834 --> 00:15:25.856
He was surprised that Dave and Solax were not bored now.

00:15:25.916 --> 00:15:30.089
Pulling in a harness was their job, and they were happy.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.128
All the dogs were alert and active.

00:15:33.188 --> 00:15:35.345
Billy was the sled dog.

00:15:35.405 --> 00:15:37.416
He was nearest to the sled.

00:15:37.476 --> 00:15:39.508
Dave was in front of him.

00:15:39.569 --> 00:15:41.190
Then there was Buck.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:43.702
In front of them were the other dogs.

00:15:43.762 --> 00:15:46.023
Spitz was the leader in front.

00:15:46.083 --> 00:15:48.875
Dave and Sallax were Buck's teachers.

00:15:48.935 --> 00:15:53.558
When Buck pulled the wrong way, Dave always bit his leg lightly.

00:15:53.618 --> 00:15:56.260
Buck learned quickly.

00:15:56.320 --> 00:16:02.914
It was a hard journey up the canyon, through sheep camp and into the mountains.

00:16:02.974 --> 00:16:06.773
That night they camped at Lake Bennett.

00:16:06.833 --> 00:16:09.814
Thousands of gold miners were there.

00:16:09.873 --> 00:16:14.975
Buck made his hole in the snow and slept well.

00:16:15.035 --> 00:16:21.316
Very early the next morning Buck and his team started pulling the sled again.

00:16:21.376 --> 00:16:26.758
That day they traveled 40 miles on a good trail.

00:16:26.818 --> 00:16:30.516
But the next day there was no trail.

00:16:30.576 --> 00:16:35.504
The dogs worked harder, and they traveled slowly.

00:16:35.564 --> 00:16:39.037
Perot usually went in front of the dogs.

00:16:39.097 --> 00:16:42.380
With his snow shoes, he made the snow flat.

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:45.381
Francois guided the sled from behind.

00:16:45.441 --> 00:16:47.342
Perot was in a hurry.

00:16:47.402 --> 00:16:51.645
He knew all about ice, and this was very important.

00:16:51.705 --> 00:16:55.618
In the fall, the ice was very thin.

00:16:55.678 --> 00:17:00.430
Day after day, Buck worked hard and pulled the sled.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:06.164
The dog started before it was light and stopped in the evening after dark.

00:17:06.224 --> 00:17:09.406
They ate a piece of fish and went to sleep.

00:17:09.466 --> 00:17:12.018
Buck was always hungry.

00:17:12.079 --> 00:17:17.972
Every day he ate a pound and a half of fish, but it was never enough.

00:17:18.032 --> 00:17:24.238
One day he saw another dog called Pike steal meat from Perot.

00:17:24.298 --> 00:17:28.678
Buck did the same the next day and no one saw him.

00:17:28.738 --> 00:17:32.216
Buck was learning to live in the hostile Northland.

00:17:32.276 --> 00:17:36.786
In the Southland, he never stole, but he was never hungry.

00:17:36.846 --> 00:17:41.347
In the Southland, there was the law of love and friendship.

00:17:41.407 --> 00:17:47.028
The man with the red sweater taught him the law of club and fang.

00:17:47.088 --> 00:17:50.039
He learned to eat all kinds of food.

00:17:50.099 --> 00:17:53.850
He learned to fight and became very clever.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:56.782
He became stronger and more primitive.

00:17:56.842 --> 00:18:01.056
The natural forces inside of him became alive.

00:18:01.116 --> 00:18:05.808
It was easy for Buck to fight like a wolf because it was in his blood.

00:18:05.868 --> 00:18:10.332
At night, he looked at a star and howled.

00:18:10.392 --> 00:18:13.994
Like his ancestors did long ago.

00:18:14.054 --> 00:18:18.356
Buck was following his instinct.

00:18:18.416 --> 00:18:27.894
Chapter 4 The Attack The primitive spirit of his ancestors was strong in Buck.

00:18:27.954 --> 00:18:32.597
And under the harsh conditions of his new life, this spirit grew.

00:18:32.617 --> 00:18:36.688
He hated Spitz more and more.

00:18:36.748 --> 00:18:39.029
But he did not want to start a fight.

00:18:39.089 --> 00:18:41.080
Buck was careful.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.801
He did nothing without thinking.

00:18:43.861 --> 00:18:46.902
Spitz always showed his teeth to Buck.

00:18:46.962 --> 00:18:48.773
He wanted to start a fight.

00:18:48.833 --> 00:18:53.203
Buck knew that a fight meant the death of one or the other.

00:18:53.263 --> 00:18:57.102
One night, the fight almost happened.

00:18:57.162 --> 00:18:59.723
They stopped at Lake La Berge.

00:18:59.783 --> 00:19:04.024
It was snowing heavily, and the wind was strong and cold.

00:19:04.084 --> 00:19:07.296
Perot and Francois made a fire on the ice.

00:19:07.356 --> 00:19:09.356
Buck made a hole in the snow.

00:19:09.416 --> 00:19:11.557
It was warm and comfortable.

00:19:11.617 --> 00:19:14.768
He did not want to leave it to get his piece of fish.

00:19:14.828 --> 00:19:21.194
When Buck finished eating the fish, he went back to his hole and found spits in it.

00:19:21.254 --> 00:19:26.720
Buck did not want to fight with Spitz, but this was too much.

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:29.332
He jumped on Spitz with great anger.

00:19:29.392 --> 00:19:31.414
Spitz was very surprised.

00:19:31.474 --> 00:19:36.196
He knew Buck was big, but he did not know he was so wild.

00:19:36.256 --> 00:19:39.268
Francois was surprised too.

00:19:39.328 --> 00:19:40.448
He cried to Buck.

00:19:40.508 --> 00:19:41.439
Give it to him!

00:19:41.499 --> 00:19:42.860
Give it to him!

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:45.021
Both dogs wanted to fight.

00:19:45.081 --> 00:19:49.326
They circled each other and waited for a chance to jump in.

00:19:49.386 --> 00:19:57.381
Suddenly, Perot shouted, and they saw about a hundred thin, hungry dogs.

00:19:57.441 --> 00:20:01.272
They came from an Indian village, and they were looking for food.

00:20:01.332 --> 00:20:07.164
Perot and Francois hit them with their clubs, but the hungry dogs showed their teeth and attacked.

00:20:07.224 --> 00:20:13.055
One dog found the food box, and in a moment, 20 dogs ate the bread and the meat.

00:20:13.115 --> 00:20:16.456
The smell of food made them crazy.

00:20:16.516 --> 00:20:22.267
The dogs looked like skeletons, with wild eyes and sharp fangs.

00:20:22.327 --> 00:20:26.118
Three of them attacked Buck and bit his head and shoulders.

00:20:26.178 --> 00:20:30.729
Dave and sulex fought courageously side by side.

00:20:30.789 --> 00:20:32.870
Joe attacked the dogs too.

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:36.601
Buck bit a dog in the neck and tasted its blood.

00:20:36.661 --> 00:20:39.161
The taste of blood made him fiercer.

00:20:39.221 --> 00:20:43.802
He jumped on another dog and then felt teeth in his own neck.

00:20:43.862 --> 00:20:46.563
Spitz was attacking him from the side.

00:20:46.623 --> 00:20:50.265
Perot and Francois came with clubs to help their dogs.

00:20:50.325 --> 00:20:54.188
The hungry dogs ran away, but only for a moment.

00:20:54.248 --> 00:20:58.621
When the two men ran back to save their food, the dogs attacked again.

00:20:58.641 --> 00:21:02.483
The terrible fight continued.

00:21:02.543 --> 00:21:08.898
Later, the nine team dogs ran away and hid in the forest.

00:21:08.958 --> 00:21:11.048
They passed the night there.

00:21:11.108 --> 00:21:17.259
Each dog was hurt in four or five places, and Joe lost his eye.

00:21:17.319 --> 00:21:21.330
Early the next morning, they slowly walked back to camp.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:23.872
Perot and Francois were angry.

00:21:23.932 --> 00:21:28.273
Half their food was gone, and one dog ate Perot's shoe.

00:21:28.333 --> 00:21:37.366
Francois looked at the poor dogs and said, Ah, my friends, perhaps those bites will make you crazy dogs.

00:21:37.426 --> 00:21:39.271
What do you think, Perot?

00:21:39.331 --> 00:21:41.406
Perot said nothing.

00:21:41.466 --> 00:21:46.270
There were four hundred miles between him and Dawson.

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:49.252
He hoped his dogs were not crazy.

00:21:49.312 --> 00:21:53.556
After two hours of hard work, the team started traveling.

00:21:53.616 --> 00:21:56.762
The next part of the trail was the most difficult.

00:21:56.822 --> 00:22:01.997
The 30-mile river was not frozen because the water moved too quickly.

00:22:02.057 --> 00:22:06.198
It took six days to travel those terrible 30 miles.

00:22:06.258 --> 00:22:13.230
They were terrible because every step was dangerous for the dogs and the men.

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:19.622
They found 12 ice bridges across the river, and Perot fell through all of them.

00:22:19.682 --> 00:22:22.337
His long stick saved him.

00:22:22.398 --> 00:22:26.985
The temperature was 50 degrees Fahrenheit below zero.

00:22:27.045 --> 00:22:33.658
Each time Perot fell into the icy water, he built a fire to dry and warm himself.

00:22:33.718 --> 00:22:37.040
Perot was not afraid of anything.

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:40.532
This is why he was a government courier.

00:22:40.592 --> 00:22:42.573
He was often in danger.

00:22:42.633 --> 00:22:47.526
Once, the sled with Buck and Dave fell through the ice.

00:22:47.586 --> 00:22:54.113
When Perot and Francois pulled them out of the river, They were covered with ice.

00:22:54.173 --> 00:23:00.635
The men built a fire to save the dogs when they arrived in Hootalinkwa.

00:23:00.695 --> 00:23:03.379
Buck and the other dogs were exhausted.

00:23:03.439 --> 00:23:07.592
However, they were late, and Perot made them run faster.

00:23:07.652 --> 00:23:14.298
In three days they traveled 110 miles and reached a place called Five Fingers.

00:23:14.358 --> 00:23:17.800
Buck's feet were not as hard as the feet of the Huskies.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:22.204
His feet were still soft because of his comfortable life with the judge.

00:23:22.264 --> 00:23:25.136
His feet hurt a lot all day.

00:23:25.196 --> 00:23:29.495
That night at the camp, he lay down like a dead dog.

00:23:29.555 --> 00:23:33.432
He was hungry, but he could not walk to get his fish.

00:23:33.492 --> 00:23:35.873
So Francois brought it to him.

00:23:35.933 --> 00:23:40.825
Every evening after dinner Francois messaged Buck's feet for half an hour.

00:23:40.885 --> 00:23:43.596
He made four little shoes for Buck.

00:23:43.656 --> 00:23:46.048
Now Buck was more comfortable.

00:23:46.108 --> 00:23:52.050
One morning Francois forgot the shoes and Buck lay on his back with his feet in the air.

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:55.102
He did not want to move without his shoes.

00:23:55.162 --> 00:24:00.402
Later his feet grew hard and the shoes were not necessary.

00:24:00.462 --> 00:24:02.824
Chapter 5.

00:24:02.884 --> 00:24:08.754
The Big Fight At Pelly River one morning Dolly suddenly went crazy.

00:24:08.814 --> 00:24:13.327
She howled like a wolf and then jumped at Buck.

00:24:13.388 --> 00:24:16.886
Buck knew this was something terrible and ran away.

00:24:16.946 --> 00:24:18.786
Dolly was behind him.

00:24:18.846 --> 00:24:20.457
Buck was afraid.

00:24:20.517 --> 00:24:26.059
He ran as fast as he could through the woods, across the ice, and back to the river.

00:24:26.119 --> 00:24:28.620
Dolly was one step behind him.

00:24:28.680 --> 00:24:31.898
Buck could hear her growling angrily.

00:24:31.958 --> 00:24:33.195
Fuck!

00:24:33.255 --> 00:24:34.726
Francois called.

00:24:34.786 --> 00:24:38.649
Francois can save me, Buck thought, and ran to him.

00:24:38.709 --> 00:24:45.794
Francois had an axe ready in his hand, as Buck ran past him, the axe fell down on Dolly's head.

00:24:45.854 --> 00:24:48.366
Buck lay down near the sled.

00:24:48.426 --> 00:24:50.156
He was exhausted.

00:24:50.216 --> 00:24:52.768
This was Spitz's opportunity.

00:24:52.828 --> 00:24:56.411
He jumped at Buck and bit him very hard.

00:24:56.471 --> 00:24:59.398
Francois saw this and hit Spitz.

00:24:59.458 --> 00:25:02.375
That Spitz is a devil, said Perot.

00:25:02.436 --> 00:25:04.918
Someday he will kill Buck.

00:25:04.978 --> 00:25:07.122
Buck is like two devils.

00:25:07.182 --> 00:25:08.904
I know this for sure.

00:25:08.964 --> 00:25:12.728
Someday Buck will get very angry and eat up Spitz.

00:25:12.788 --> 00:25:14.370
Francois said.

00:25:14.430 --> 00:25:19.464
From then on, it was war between Spitz and Buck.

00:25:19.524 --> 00:25:23.216
Spitz was the lead dog and master of the team.

00:25:23.276 --> 00:25:25.948
Buck wanted to be the lead dog.

00:25:26.008 --> 00:25:28.020
It was part of his nature.

00:25:28.080 --> 00:25:31.012
Spitz knew this and hated him.

00:25:31.072 --> 00:25:35.516
Buck was dangerous because he was strong, clever, and patient.

00:25:35.577 --> 00:25:40.110
When the dogs made mistakes, Buck protected them from Spitz.

00:25:40.170 --> 00:25:46.226
One morning, Pike did not want to get up, and Spitz looked for him everywhere.

00:25:46.286 --> 00:25:51.630
When he found Pike, he jumped at him, but Buck suddenly attacked Spitz.

00:25:51.690 --> 00:25:55.502
Francois whipped Buck with all his strength.

00:25:55.562 --> 00:25:57.844
This did not stop Buck.

00:25:57.904 --> 00:26:01.226
Francois whipped him again and again.

00:26:01.286 --> 00:26:06.146
The other dogs saw this and it became difficult for Spitz to lead them.

00:26:06.206 --> 00:26:10.766
day after day Buck protected the other dogs from Spitz.

00:26:10.826 --> 00:26:14.308
Buck did it secretly when Francois was not looking.

00:26:14.368 --> 00:26:17.592
Things began to change on the team.

00:26:17.652 --> 00:26:20.864
The dogs did not respect or obey Spitz.

00:26:20.924 --> 00:26:22.986
The team became worse.

00:26:23.046 --> 00:26:28.150
There was always more trouble and Buck was responsible for it.

00:26:28.210 --> 00:26:31.372
Francois was worried about Buck and Spitz.

00:26:31.432 --> 00:26:34.594
Those dogs will have a big fight one day.

00:26:34.654 --> 00:26:35.706
He thought.

00:26:35.766 --> 00:26:38.848
but the days passed without a big fight.

00:26:38.908 --> 00:26:43.330
They arrived in Dawson City on a cold, gray afternoon.

00:26:43.390 --> 00:26:46.591
There were many men and dogs in Dawson.

00:26:46.651 --> 00:26:49.082
The dogs did all kinds of work.

00:26:49.142 --> 00:26:54.364
Buck met some Southland dogs, but most of the dogs were Huskies.

00:26:54.424 --> 00:27:03.840
At night, there was the Aurora Borealis and the stars danced in the sky every night at nine o'clock.

00:27:03.901 --> 00:27:11.060
at twelve, and at three, all the dogs howled together.

00:27:11.120 --> 00:27:14.034
Buck liked to howl with them.

00:27:14.094 --> 00:27:18.620
It was a strange song of the night from thousands of years ago.

00:27:18.680 --> 00:27:21.842
It was the song of Buck's ancestors.

00:27:21.903 --> 00:27:25.356
It was about the difficulties of life.

00:27:25.416 --> 00:27:28.628
They left Dawson after seven days.

00:27:28.688 --> 00:27:30.970
Perot had some important letters.

00:27:31.030 --> 00:27:34.752
He wanted to return to Dai'i as fast as possible.

00:27:34.812 --> 00:27:38.346
The dogs were rested and in good condition.

00:27:38.406 --> 00:27:45.537
On the first day they traveled fifty miles, and on the second day they were on the Yukon River near Peli.

00:27:45.597 --> 00:27:48.483
Francois had many problems with the team.

00:27:48.543 --> 00:27:51.264
The dogs did not work well together.

00:27:51.324 --> 00:27:53.705
Buck and Spitz hated each other.

00:27:53.765 --> 00:27:56.426
The other dogs did not respect Spitz.

00:27:56.486 --> 00:27:59.118
They were not afraid of him anymore.

00:27:59.178 --> 00:28:04.319
Francois often stopped the sled because the dogs were fighting.

00:28:04.380 --> 00:28:08.011
Francois knew that Buck caused the trouble.

00:28:08.071 --> 00:28:12.928
But Buck was very clever, and Francois never saw him.

00:28:12.988 --> 00:28:17.383
Buck worked hard and he loved pulling the sled.

00:28:17.443 --> 00:28:21.934
One night after dinner, Dubb found a snow rabbit.

00:28:21.994 --> 00:28:25.206
In a moment all the dogs were running after it.

00:28:25.266 --> 00:28:30.057
Nearby there was a camp of the Northwest Police with fifty dogs.

00:28:30.117 --> 00:28:33.528
The fifty dogs started running after the rabbit too.

00:28:33.588 --> 00:28:36.729
The rabbit ran quickly on the soft snow.

00:28:36.789 --> 00:28:39.320
But it was more difficult for the dogs.

00:28:39.380 --> 00:28:43.532
Buck led the pack of sixty dogs and he was very happy.

00:28:43.592 --> 00:28:47.314
He was hunting his food and he felt alive.

00:28:47.374 --> 00:28:51.596
His splendid body moved forward in the white moonlight.

00:28:51.656 --> 00:28:54.899
In the end, Spitz caught the rabbit.

00:28:54.959 --> 00:28:58.351
He broke its back with his teeth and threw it in the air.

00:28:58.411 --> 00:29:00.232
Buck attacked Spitz.

00:29:00.292 --> 00:29:02.394
The dogs fell in the snow.

00:29:02.454 --> 00:29:05.866
Spitz bit Buck twice and then jumped away.

00:29:05.926 --> 00:29:08.178
He watched Buck carefully.

00:29:08.238 --> 00:29:11.019
Buck knew this was the big fight.

00:29:11.080 --> 00:29:14.522
Either he or Spitz must die.

00:29:14.582 --> 00:29:18.339
Their ears went back and they growled angrily.

00:29:18.359 --> 00:29:22.746
They watched each other carefully and they circled slowly.

00:29:22.766 --> 00:29:28.448
The night was silent and everything was white in the moonlight.

00:29:28.509 --> 00:29:33.445
The other dogs ate the rabbit and then turned to watch the fight.

00:29:33.506 --> 00:29:37.158
Spitz was a great fighter and he was intelligent.

00:29:37.218 --> 00:29:41.751
Buck tried to bite his throat, but Spitz always defended himself.

00:29:41.811 --> 00:29:46.634
Every time Buck attacked, Spitz moved away and bit him on the side.

00:29:46.694 --> 00:29:49.366
Soon Buck was covered with blood.

00:29:49.426 --> 00:29:51.378
The fight was desperate.

00:29:51.438 --> 00:29:53.789
But Buck had a good imagination.

00:29:53.849 --> 00:29:57.422
He fought with his instinct, but also with his head.

00:29:57.482 --> 00:29:59.743
Buck attacked again.

00:29:59.803 --> 00:30:04.785
But at the last minute, he went under Spitz and bit his left leg.

00:30:04.845 --> 00:30:08.726
The bone broke and Spitz stood on three legs.

00:30:08.786 --> 00:30:13.108
Buck attacked three more times and then broke his right leg.

00:30:13.168 --> 00:30:15.548
There was no hope for Spitz now.

00:30:15.608 --> 00:30:19.400
The silent circle of dogs moved closer to Spitz.

00:30:19.460 --> 00:30:21.956
They waited for the end.

00:30:22.016 --> 00:30:24.112
Then Buck attacked again.

00:30:24.172 --> 00:30:26.703
Spitz fell down on the snow.

00:30:26.764 --> 00:30:30.658
He disappeared under the circle of the other dogs.

00:30:30.718 --> 00:30:33.390
Buck stood and watched.

00:30:33.450 --> 00:30:37.154
He was the champion.

00:30:37.214 --> 00:30:41.246
Exercise 2, listening.

00:30:41.306 --> 00:30:42.378
Hello!

00:30:42.398 --> 00:30:46.452
I want to write an article about couriers in the Yukon territory.

00:30:46.512 --> 00:30:48.062
What does a courier do?

00:30:48.122 --> 00:30:54.393
Well, I take important government papers and documents from Diye to Dawson City.

00:30:54.453 --> 00:30:57.054
What time do you start traveling in the morning?

00:30:57.114 --> 00:31:02.318
I wake up at six o'clock, honest to dogs, and start traveling at half past six.

00:31:02.378 --> 00:31:05.359
Well, there's a very cold in the Yukon territory.

00:31:05.419 --> 00:31:06.319
Oh, yes.

00:31:06.380 --> 00:31:10.172
The temperature is about 50 degrees Fahrenheit below zero.

00:31:10.232 --> 00:31:12.152
Do you stop to have lunch?

00:31:12.212 --> 00:31:14.294
No, we don't have time.

00:31:14.354 --> 00:31:16.602
When do you stop to eat and rest?

00:31:16.663 --> 00:31:19.242
We stop at seven o'clock in the evening.

00:31:19.302 --> 00:31:20.633
What do you eat?

00:31:20.693 --> 00:31:22.935
Frostwell and I eat bread and fish.

00:31:22.995 --> 00:31:24.876
The dogs eat only fish.

00:31:24.936 --> 00:31:26.878
When did you leave Dye?

00:31:26.938 --> 00:31:29.911
We left on Thursday, December 6.

00:31:29.971 --> 00:31:32.393
When did you arrive in Dawson City?

00:31:32.453 --> 00:31:35.506
We arrived on Sunday, December 30.

00:31:35.566 --> 00:31:37.298
Do you like your job?

00:31:37.358 --> 00:31:40.460
Yes, it's very exciting.

00:31:40.520 --> 00:31:52.152
Chapter 6 The New Lee Dog The next morning, Francois could not find Spitz, and he saw Buck covered with blood.

00:31:52.212 --> 00:31:53.442
What did I say?

00:31:53.502 --> 00:31:56.363
Buck is a great fighter, said Francois.

00:31:56.423 --> 00:32:05.375
Perot looked at the wounds on Buck's body and said, That Spitz fought like a devil, and Buck fought like two devils, Francois said.

00:32:05.435 --> 00:32:07.135
Now we can travel faster.

00:32:07.195 --> 00:32:09.808
No more Spitz, no more trouble.

00:32:09.868 --> 00:32:13.272
Francois started to harness the dogs.

00:32:13.332 --> 00:32:16.294
Buck walked to Spitz's old position.

00:32:16.354 --> 00:32:19.847
But Francois put Sallax in the lead position.

00:32:19.908 --> 00:32:23.180
Buck jumped angrily at Sallax.

00:32:23.240 --> 00:32:25.852
Francois cried, look at that Buck.

00:32:25.912 --> 00:32:29.466
He killed Spitz and now he wants his place.

00:32:29.526 --> 00:32:31.287
Go away Buck.

00:32:31.347 --> 00:32:34.160
But Buck did not move.

00:32:34.220 --> 00:32:36.471
Sallax was not happy.

00:32:36.532 --> 00:32:38.428
He was afraid of Buck.

00:32:38.488 --> 00:32:43.486
When Francois turned his back, Buck pushed Sallak's way.

00:32:43.547 --> 00:32:45.718
Francois was angry.

00:32:45.778 --> 00:32:47.580
Now I'll show you.

00:32:47.640 --> 00:32:49.932
He went to get a heavy club.

00:32:49.992 --> 00:32:53.784
Buck remembered the man in the red sweater and moved away.

00:32:53.844 --> 00:32:54.946
Come here Buck.

00:32:55.006 --> 00:32:56.376
Said Francois.

00:32:56.436 --> 00:32:57.908
Buck did not obey.

00:32:57.928 --> 00:33:02.672
He wanted to be the lead dog because he won the fight with spits.

00:33:02.732 --> 00:33:07.282
The two men tried to put on the harness, but he always moved away.

00:33:07.342 --> 00:33:08.618
Come here Buck."

00:33:08.678 --> 00:33:09.768
Perot said.

00:33:09.828 --> 00:33:12.479
But Buck did not move.

00:33:12.539 --> 00:33:14.120
It was late.

00:33:14.180 --> 00:33:17.541
Francois put solace in his old place.

00:33:17.601 --> 00:33:20.832
Perot looked at his watch and he was angry.

00:33:20.892 --> 00:33:22.862
Put down the club, Francois.

00:33:22.922 --> 00:33:27.854
Francois put down the club and Buck came to the front of the team.

00:33:27.914 --> 00:33:32.947
Francois put on the harness and the sled started moving.

00:33:33.007 --> 00:33:36.090
Buck was an excellently dog.

00:33:36.150 --> 00:33:38.550
He moved and thought quickly.

00:33:38.610 --> 00:33:41.211
The other dogs worked harder with Buck.

00:33:41.271 --> 00:33:44.081
The team traveled faster and faster.

00:33:44.141 --> 00:33:47.172
Buck is the best dog, the very best.

00:33:47.232 --> 00:33:48.862
Francois said.

00:33:48.922 --> 00:33:52.973
It was 45 degrees fahrenheit below zero.

00:33:53.033 --> 00:33:56.744
Some days the dogs traveled 60 miles or more.

00:33:56.804 --> 00:34:00.755
After 14 days, they reached Skagway.

00:34:00.815 --> 00:34:03.869
The dog team was the center of attention.

00:34:03.929 --> 00:34:07.604
Then the two men received orders from the Canadian government.

00:34:07.664 --> 00:34:11.290
Francois put his arms around Buck and cried.

00:34:11.350 --> 00:34:16.386
Then the two men left, and Buck did not see them again.

00:34:16.446 --> 00:34:20.068
Another man took Buck and his team back to Dawson.

00:34:20.128 --> 00:34:24.771
The sled was very heavy because it carried mail for the gold miners.

00:34:24.832 --> 00:34:29.054
Buck did not like it, but he and the other dogs worked hard.

00:34:29.115 --> 00:34:31.616
It was not an interesting life.

00:34:31.676 --> 00:34:34.077
One day was like another.

00:34:34.138 --> 00:34:36.608
They started before it was light.

00:34:36.668 --> 00:34:40.788
At night they camped, and this was the best part of the day.

00:34:40.848 --> 00:34:44.219
The dogs ate some fish and rested by the fire.

00:34:44.280 --> 00:34:46.900
Bucked love to rest by the fire.

00:34:46.960 --> 00:34:51.541
Sometimes he thought of Judge Miller's big house and his life there.

00:34:51.601 --> 00:34:58.044
He also thought about the man in the red sweater, the death of Curly, and the big fight with spits.

00:34:58.104 --> 00:35:05.434
Other times he remembered his parents, his ancestors, and the world of long ago.

00:35:05.454 --> 00:35:09.990
The journey was hard, and the mail was heavy.

00:35:10.050 --> 00:35:12.512
The dogs were tired and weak.

00:35:12.572 --> 00:35:14.683
They needed a long rest.

00:35:14.743 --> 00:35:18.284
But after only two days, they were traveling again.

00:35:18.344 --> 00:35:20.856
The dogs and the men were unhappy.

00:35:20.916 --> 00:35:24.027
Each night, the men took care of their dogs.

00:35:24.087 --> 00:35:28.159
They looked at their feet, but the dogs became weaker every day.

00:35:28.219 --> 00:35:32.061
Billy cried in his sleep and was very unfriendly.

00:35:32.121 --> 00:35:34.391
Dave was tired and ill.

00:35:34.452 --> 00:35:36.572
Something was wrong with him.

00:35:36.632 --> 00:35:41.719
When they stopped in the evening, he lay down and did not stand up until morning.

00:35:41.779 --> 00:35:44.144
The men were worried about Dave.

00:35:44.204 --> 00:35:46.815
They did not understand his illness.

00:35:46.875 --> 00:35:50.997
One day, Dave could not pull the sled anymore.

00:35:51.057 --> 00:35:54.338
He cried sadly when Solax took his place.

00:35:54.399 --> 00:35:57.760
The next morning, Dave could not move.

00:35:57.820 --> 00:36:01.232
The driver took his pistol and walked away.

00:36:01.252 --> 00:36:05.154
The dogs heard a shot.

00:36:05.214 --> 00:36:09.885
The man came back quickly, and the sled moved again.

00:36:09.945 --> 00:36:13.455
Buck and the other dogs knew what happened to Dave.

00:36:13.515 --> 00:36:19.086
Thirty days after leaving Dawson City, the team arrived in Scagway.

00:36:19.147 --> 00:36:21.817
The dogs were exhausted and thin.

00:36:21.877 --> 00:36:23.978
They needed a long rest.

00:36:24.038 --> 00:36:27.929
The men needed new, strong dogs to pull the sled.

00:36:27.989 --> 00:36:30.840
They sold the old tired dogs.

00:36:30.900 --> 00:36:35.867
Two American men called Hal and Charles bought Buck and his team.

00:36:35.927 --> 00:36:38.234
They bought other dogs too.

00:36:38.294 --> 00:36:42.754
Charles was forty years old, and Hal was a young man.

00:36:42.814 --> 00:36:46.596
Charles's wife, Mercedes, was also with them.

00:36:46.656 --> 00:36:52.107
They knew nothing about life in the Northland, and they made many mistakes.

00:36:52.167 --> 00:36:56.828
They put too many things on their sled and tried to start.

00:36:56.888 --> 00:37:02.199
The dogs pulled hard for a few moments, and then stopped.

00:37:02.259 --> 00:37:06.239
They could not move because it was too heavy.

00:37:06.300 --> 00:37:08.190
These lazy animals?

00:37:08.250 --> 00:37:10.583
Cried howl with a whip in his hand.

00:37:10.643 --> 00:37:12.906
That very weak said a man.

00:37:12.966 --> 00:37:14.408
They need a rest.

00:37:14.468 --> 00:37:16.760
Nonsense, they're very lazy.

00:37:16.820 --> 00:37:17.811
Said howl.

00:37:17.871 --> 00:37:18.552
Mosh!

00:37:18.612 --> 00:37:19.593
He cried.

00:37:19.653 --> 00:37:20.856
Mosh!

00:37:20.916 --> 00:37:24.480
Hal whipped the dogs again and again.

00:37:24.540 --> 00:37:29.363
Another man said, I don't care about you, but I care about the dogs.

00:37:29.423 --> 00:37:33.346
Break the ice around the sled, and then the dogs can pull.

00:37:33.406 --> 00:37:37.520
Hal broke the ice, and the sled moved forward.

00:37:37.580 --> 00:37:40.722
The unhappy team moved on.

00:37:40.782 --> 00:37:44.915
Day after day, Hal whipped the poor dogs.

00:37:44.975 --> 00:37:47.186
He gave them little food to eat.

00:37:47.246 --> 00:37:50.136
They were very tired and very hungry.

00:37:50.196 --> 00:37:52.238
They looked like skeletons.

00:37:52.298 --> 00:37:54.840
Dubbed hurt himself and was shot.

00:37:54.900 --> 00:37:57.681
Billy and some other dogs died.

00:37:57.742 --> 00:38:00.874
Soon we will all die.

00:38:00.934 --> 00:38:03.175
Buck thought.

00:38:03.235 --> 00:38:12.451
CHAPTER VII FOR THE LOVE OF A MAN Only five dogs reach John Thornton's camp.

00:38:12.511 --> 00:38:16.170
Joe, Pike, Salt Lake's teak and Buck.

00:38:16.230 --> 00:38:19.829
They fell on the ground, and could not move.

00:38:19.889 --> 00:38:22.029
They were almost dead.

00:38:22.089 --> 00:38:26.910
It was nearly the end of winter, and it was a beautiful day.

00:38:26.970 --> 00:38:29.600
John Thornton was repairing an axe.

00:38:29.660 --> 00:38:31.701
Is it safe to cross the river here?

00:38:31.761 --> 00:38:32.841
asked Hal.

00:38:32.901 --> 00:38:35.001
Oh no, it's very dangerous.

00:38:35.061 --> 00:38:36.422
The ice is too thin.

00:38:36.482 --> 00:38:38.072
Answered Thornton.

00:38:38.132 --> 00:38:41.603
Hal looked at him and said, I don't believe you.

00:38:41.663 --> 00:38:43.264
We must go to Dawson.

00:38:43.324 --> 00:38:47.448
He took his whip and cried, Come on Buck, let's go!

00:38:47.509 --> 00:38:52.282
Thornton knew these people were stupid and did not understand.

00:38:52.342 --> 00:38:54.542
The team did not move.

00:38:54.602 --> 00:38:58.015
After a while, Solic slowly stood up.

00:38:58.075 --> 00:39:00.696
Joe was crying but he stood up.

00:39:00.756 --> 00:39:03.998
Pike tried twice and fell down.

00:39:04.058 --> 00:39:06.020
The third time he stood up.

00:39:06.080 --> 00:39:07.971
Buck did not try.

00:39:08.031 --> 00:39:11.418
Hal whipped him but Buck did not move.

00:39:11.478 --> 00:39:14.405
Thornton wanted to speak, but he did not.

00:39:14.465 --> 00:39:17.177
Hal was furious and took the club.

00:39:17.237 --> 00:39:20.369
He hit Buck again and again.

00:39:20.429 --> 00:39:23.311
But Buck did not want to stand up.

00:39:23.371 --> 00:39:26.284
He had a strange feeling of doom.

00:39:26.344 --> 00:39:29.166
He saw thin ice in front of him.

00:39:29.226 --> 00:39:34.439
After so much suffering, he did not feel the club.

00:39:34.499 --> 00:39:38.720
Then suddenly Thornton jumped on Hal and threw him to the ground.

00:39:38.781 --> 00:39:41.551
Don't hit that dog again or I'll kill you.

00:39:41.611 --> 00:39:42.882
Thornton cried.

00:39:42.942 --> 00:39:45.043
It's my dog, said Hal.

00:39:45.103 --> 00:39:46.894
Go away or I'll hit you too.

00:39:46.955 --> 00:39:48.426
I'm going to Dawson.

00:39:48.486 --> 00:39:51.288
Thornton stood between him and Buck.

00:39:51.348 --> 00:39:53.940
Hal took out his long knife.

00:39:54.000 --> 00:39:56.661
Thornton knocked it out of Hal's hand.

00:39:56.721 --> 00:40:00.704
Then Thornton picked it up and cut Buck's harness.

00:40:00.764 --> 00:40:02.866
Hal did not want to fight.

00:40:02.926 --> 00:40:04.516
Buck was almost dead.

00:40:04.576 --> 00:40:08.217
A few minutes later, Hal and the sled went along the river.

00:40:08.277 --> 00:40:14.188
Buck raised his head and saw Pike, Solix, Joe, and Teak pulling the sled.

00:40:14.248 --> 00:40:16.629
Thornton examined Buck's body.

00:40:16.689 --> 00:40:19.020
He was looking for broken bones.

00:40:19.080 --> 00:40:22.200
Buck was terribly thin and weak.

00:40:22.261 --> 00:40:26.602
You have many wounds, but no broken bones.

00:40:26.662 --> 00:40:28.126
Said Thornton.

00:40:28.186 --> 00:40:31.762
Both Dog and Man watched the sled.

00:40:31.822 --> 00:40:34.866
It was crossing the ice in the middle of the river.

00:40:34.926 --> 00:40:38.899
Suddenly the back of the sled went down and the front went up.

00:40:38.919 --> 00:40:41.260
There was a lot of screaming.

00:40:41.280 --> 00:40:47.376
Then a big piece of ice broke and the dogs and the people disappeared.

00:40:47.436 --> 00:40:51.259
John Thornton and Buck looked at each other.

00:40:51.319 --> 00:40:52.880
You poor dog.

00:40:52.940 --> 00:40:56.484
Said Thornton and Buck licked his hand.

00:40:56.544 --> 00:40:59.656
John Thornton was ill all winter.

00:40:59.716 --> 00:41:03.467
His friends left him at White River while they went to Dawson.

00:41:03.528 --> 00:41:07.310
Thornton had a lot of food and he was comfortable.

00:41:07.370 --> 00:41:10.802
Now it was spring and he was better.

00:41:10.862 --> 00:41:15.264
During the warm spring days, he and Buck sacked by the river.

00:41:15.324 --> 00:41:19.446
Buck watched the water and listened to the birds.

00:41:19.506 --> 00:41:22.068
He needed the long rest.

00:41:22.128 --> 00:41:25.907
Slowly he became stronger and fatter.

00:41:25.967 --> 00:41:29.375
John Thornton had two other dogs.

00:41:29.435 --> 00:41:33.646
Skeet was a small dog and she made friends with Buck.

00:41:33.706 --> 00:41:36.526
When Buck was ill she took care of him.

00:41:36.587 --> 00:41:39.237
She washed his cuts with her tongue.

00:41:39.297 --> 00:41:42.198
Nigg was a big friendly dog.

00:41:42.258 --> 00:41:47.279
His eyes laughed when Buck became stronger the three dogs played together.

00:41:47.339 --> 00:41:50.031
Thornton sometimes played with them.

00:41:50.091 --> 00:41:52.534
The days passed happily.

00:41:52.594 --> 00:41:56.286
For the first time, Buck learned to love.

00:41:56.346 --> 00:42:01.170
He and Judge Miller were very good friends, but Buck did not love him.

00:42:01.230 --> 00:42:06.606
John Thornton saved Buck's life, and he was the perfect master.

00:42:06.666 --> 00:42:10.168
He loved his dogs and took good care of them.

00:42:10.228 --> 00:42:12.530
The dogs were like his children.

00:42:12.590 --> 00:42:14.592
He always talked to Buck.

00:42:14.652 --> 00:42:18.633
He took Buck's head between his hands and shook it lovingly.

00:42:18.693 --> 00:42:20.632
He adored Thornton.

00:42:20.692 --> 00:42:25.683
When Thornton touched him or spoke to him, he was wild with happiness.

00:42:25.743 --> 00:42:29.494
He sat near Thornton and looked at his face for hours.

00:42:29.554 --> 00:42:32.685
At first Buck followed Thornton everywhere.

00:42:32.745 --> 00:42:36.816
He did not want Thornton to leave like Francois and Perot.

00:42:36.877 --> 00:42:41.878
Buck was very happy with Thornton, but he was a dog of the Northland.

00:42:41.938 --> 00:42:46.289
He dreamed of other animals and heard them calling him.

00:42:46.349 --> 00:42:49.206
It was the call of the wild.

00:42:49.266 --> 00:42:53.072
Sometimes Buck wanted to answer the call.

00:42:53.132 --> 00:42:58.406
He often went into the forest, but he always returned to Thornton.

00:42:58.466 --> 00:43:01.117
Buck was not interested in other men.

00:43:01.177 --> 00:43:06.730
When Thornton's friends Hans and Pete returned, Buck did not notice them.

00:43:06.790 --> 00:43:11.042
He knew there were Thornton's good friends, and so he accepted them.

00:43:11.102 --> 00:43:15.814
Hans and Pete saw that Buck loved only Thornton and no one else.

00:43:15.874 --> 00:43:18.983
He was always happy to obey Thornton.

00:43:19.043 --> 00:43:22.392
One day, they were in Circle City.

00:43:22.452 --> 00:43:26.424
Black Burton was a bad and cruel man.

00:43:26.484 --> 00:43:30.017
He was in a saloon and he was fighting with another man.

00:43:30.077 --> 00:43:32.268
Thornton tried to stop them.

00:43:32.328 --> 00:43:34.670
Buck sat in a corner and watched.

00:43:34.730 --> 00:43:37.572
Burton hit Thornton and he almost fell.

00:43:37.632 --> 00:43:39.603
It was a loud growl.

00:43:39.663 --> 00:43:42.615
And Buck jumped into the air at Burton's throat.

00:43:42.675 --> 00:43:45.377
The man put up his arm and saved his life.

00:43:45.437 --> 00:43:48.589
Then he fell to the ground with Buck on top of him.

00:43:48.649 --> 00:43:50.670
Buck bit into his throat.

00:43:50.730 --> 00:43:53.262
Some people pulled Buck off the man.

00:43:53.322 --> 00:43:56.365
A doctor arrived and examined Burton's throat.

00:43:56.425 --> 00:43:59.217
Dog attacked, only because Thorne was in danger.

00:43:59.277 --> 00:44:00.508
Someone said.

00:44:00.568 --> 00:44:06.230
From that day, Buck's name became famous all over the Northland.

00:44:06.290 --> 00:44:11.309
In the fall of that year, Buck saved Thornton's life another time.

00:44:11.369 --> 00:44:13.779
The three men were going down the river.

00:44:13.839 --> 00:44:18.040
Thornton was in the boat and Hans and Pete were on the river bank.

00:44:18.100 --> 00:44:20.370
They were holding the boat with a rope.

00:44:20.431 --> 00:44:23.211
Buck was on the bank and watched his master.

00:44:23.271 --> 00:44:26.222
Soon they came to a dangerous part of the river.

00:44:26.282 --> 00:44:30.092
The boat was going too fast because the current was strong.

00:44:30.152 --> 00:44:33.963
Hans pulled the rope to stop the boat, but it turned over.

00:44:34.023 --> 00:44:36.325
Thornton fell into the water.

00:44:36.385 --> 00:44:40.248
Buck jumped in immediately and swam to his master.

00:44:40.308 --> 00:44:48.956
Thornton took Buck's tail and Buck swam bravely towards the riverbank, but they moved slowly because the river pushed them to the rocks.

00:44:49.016 --> 00:44:53.982
We can't get to the riverbank, because the current is too strong," said Thornton.

00:44:54.042 --> 00:44:57.576
He held onto a rock and let go of Buck's tail.

00:44:57.636 --> 00:45:00.290
Then he cried, go Buck, go!

00:45:00.350 --> 00:45:03.154
Buck obeyed and swam to the riverbank.

00:45:03.214 --> 00:45:05.810
Hands and Pete pulled him out of the river.

00:45:05.870 --> 00:45:08.004
We must work fast to save Thornton.

00:45:08.064 --> 00:45:10.306
He's in great danger," said Pete.

00:45:10.366 --> 00:45:14.470
They tied a rope around Buck, and he jumped into the river again.

00:45:14.530 --> 00:45:18.382
The river carried him past Thornton, but he finally reached him.

00:45:18.442 --> 00:45:23.547
Thornton held on to Buck, and Hans and Pete pulled the rope very hard.

00:45:23.608 --> 00:45:26.800
Thornton and Buck disappeared under the water.

00:45:26.860 --> 00:45:30.987
When Hans and Pete pulled them out, they both seemed dead.

00:45:31.048 --> 00:45:33.994
but they slowly opened their eyes.

00:45:34.054 --> 00:45:38.886
Thornton examined Buck's body and found three broken bones.

00:45:38.946 --> 00:45:44.208
We must camp here until Buck is better, said Thornton.

00:45:44.268 --> 00:45:54.384
Chapter 8 The Winner At Dawson that winner, Buck did something that made him very famous in the Northland.

00:45:54.444 --> 00:46:00.994
Thornton Hans and Pete wanted to go to the east to look for gold, but they needed money.

00:46:01.054 --> 00:46:04.734
One day, they were at the El Dorado saloon.

00:46:04.794 --> 00:46:08.516
My dog can pull a sled with 500 pounds on it.

00:46:08.576 --> 00:46:09.816
Said one man.

00:46:09.876 --> 00:46:13.208
Well, my dog can pull 600 pounds.

00:46:13.268 --> 00:46:14.558
Said another man.

00:46:14.618 --> 00:46:15.329
Really?

00:46:15.389 --> 00:46:18.080
Well, my dog can pull 700 pounds.

00:46:18.140 --> 00:46:20.692
Said a third man called Mathewson.

00:46:20.752 --> 00:46:22.082
That's nothing.

00:46:22.142 --> 00:46:23.290
Said Thornton.

00:46:23.350 --> 00:46:25.537
Buck can pull a thousand pounds.

00:46:25.597 --> 00:46:29.889
Can he move the sled when it's frozen to the ice and then pull it a hundred yards?"

00:46:29.949 --> 00:46:31.150
asked Mathewson.

00:46:31.210 --> 00:46:32.540
Yes, he can.

00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:33.851
Said Thornton.

00:46:33.911 --> 00:46:34.792
Well?

00:46:34.852 --> 00:46:36.142
Said Mathewson.

00:46:36.202 --> 00:46:39.614
I've got a thousand dollars here and I say he can't.

00:46:39.674 --> 00:46:43.616
He took a bag of gold and put it on the table.

00:46:43.676 --> 00:46:45.517
Nobody spoke.

00:46:45.577 --> 00:46:52.112
Thornton thought, I know Buck is strong, but is he really so strong?

00:46:52.172 --> 00:46:56.118
The men at the saloon looked at him silently and waited.

00:46:56.178 --> 00:47:01.511
Thornton did not have a thousand dollars, and his friends did not either.

00:47:01.571 --> 00:47:04.543
I've got a sled outside with a thousand pounds on it.

00:47:04.603 --> 00:47:05.824
Mathewson said.

00:47:05.884 --> 00:47:07.444
Do you want to try?

00:47:07.504 --> 00:47:10.176
Thornton did not know what to say.

00:47:10.236 --> 00:47:12.338
He looked at all the men.

00:47:12.398 --> 00:47:16.100
Then he saw his old friend, Jim O'Brien.

00:47:16.160 --> 00:47:18.572
Can you lend me a thousand dollars, Jim?

00:47:18.632 --> 00:47:20.526
Thornton said softly.

00:47:20.586 --> 00:47:22.510
Sure, said O'Brien.

00:47:22.571 --> 00:47:24.912
But I don't think your dog can do it.

00:47:24.972 --> 00:47:27.414
Everyone went into the street.

00:47:27.474 --> 00:47:30.748
A lot of men stood around Mathewson sled.

00:47:30.808 --> 00:47:35.342
The sled was frozen to the ice because it was terribly cold.

00:47:35.402 --> 00:47:40.676
Mathewson was sure Buck could not win and said, I'm paying another $400.

00:47:40.696 --> 00:47:42.259
What about you?

00:47:42.319 --> 00:47:47.074
Thornton, Hans, and Pete talked together.

00:47:47.134 --> 00:47:52.668
They had only two hundred dollars, and they added them to the thousand dollars.

00:47:52.728 --> 00:47:55.750
Buck felt the excitement in the air.

00:47:55.810 --> 00:47:59.974
He knew he must do something great for Thornton.

00:48:00.034 --> 00:48:02.266
Buck was in perfect condition.

00:48:02.326 --> 00:48:04.778
He was a splendid dog.

00:48:04.838 --> 00:48:08.290
Thornton sat down on the snow next to Buck.

00:48:08.350 --> 00:48:13.138
He held Buck's head in his hands and spoke softly in his ear.

00:48:13.198 --> 00:48:15.194
If you love me, Buck.

00:48:15.254 --> 00:48:17.096
If you love me."

00:48:17.156 --> 00:48:19.068
Buck understood.

00:48:19.128 --> 00:48:23.730
He took Thornton's hand between his teeth and then let go.

00:48:23.790 --> 00:48:26.903
He often did this as a sign of his love.

00:48:26.963 --> 00:48:28.964
Everyone was silent.

00:48:29.024 --> 00:48:31.937
Thornton stood up and said, ready Buck?

00:48:31.997 --> 00:48:34.088
Buck pulled on the harness.

00:48:34.149 --> 00:48:34.939
Right!

00:48:34.999 --> 00:48:36.466
cried Thornton.

00:48:36.526 --> 00:48:39.814
Buck pulled to the right and stopped suddenly.

00:48:39.874 --> 00:48:40.954
Now left!

00:48:41.014 --> 00:48:42.214
cried Thornton.

00:48:42.274 --> 00:48:44.035
Buck pulled to the left.

00:48:44.095 --> 00:48:45.846
The ice was breaking.

00:48:45.906 --> 00:48:47.926
Now, mush!

00:48:47.986 --> 00:48:49.877
Buck started to pull.

00:48:49.937 --> 00:48:52.638
His strong body pulled harder and harder.

00:48:52.698 --> 00:48:54.748
The sled moved a little.

00:48:54.808 --> 00:48:58.440
Suddenly, it started to go forward on the snow.

00:48:58.500 --> 00:49:01.730
Buck pulled it for 100 yards.

00:49:01.790 --> 00:49:03.551
He was the winner.

00:49:03.611 --> 00:49:06.918
The men shouted and threw their hats in the air.

00:49:06.978 --> 00:49:09.795
Buck Thornton was on the snow with Buck.

00:49:09.855 --> 00:49:11.826
He took his head and shook it.

00:49:11.886 --> 00:49:14.008
He was crying with happiness.

00:49:14.068 --> 00:49:17.080
Buck had Thornton's hand between his teeth.

00:49:17.140 --> 00:49:23.676
In five minutes, Buck made $1,600 for Thornton and his friends.

00:49:23.736 --> 00:49:29.250
With this money, they could travel to the east to look for a lost gold mine.

00:49:29.310 --> 00:49:31.252
No one knew where it was.

00:49:31.312 --> 00:49:33.040
It was a mystery.

00:49:33.100 --> 00:49:37.430
The three men with Buck and six other dogs started to go east.

00:49:37.490 --> 00:49:42.343
They traveled up the Stewart River and into the Mackenzie Mountains.

00:49:42.403 --> 00:49:45.244
Thornton was not afraid of the wild.

00:49:45.304 --> 00:49:47.636
He hunted his food during the day.

00:49:47.696 --> 00:49:49.277
Buck was very happy.

00:49:49.337 --> 00:49:52.118
He loved hunting, fishing and traveling.

00:49:52.178 --> 00:49:55.850
They camped in different places and looked for gold.

00:49:55.910 --> 00:50:01.634
In the summer they built small boats and crossed mountain lakes and went down rivers.

00:50:01.694 --> 00:50:06.624
The months passed and they continued to travel in the unknown country.

00:50:06.684 --> 00:50:12.516
In the winter they found an old cabin, but they did not find the gold mine.

00:50:12.576 --> 00:50:17.537
Then in the spring they found a stream with gold in it.

00:50:17.597 --> 00:50:19.737
It looked like yellow butter.

00:50:19.798 --> 00:50:23.928
Every day the men worked hard and found lots of gold.

00:50:23.988 --> 00:50:26.789
They put it in many big bags.

00:50:26.849 --> 00:50:30.388
Each bag had fifty pounds of gold.

00:50:30.448 --> 00:50:34.308
The dogs did nothing except watch the men and eat.

00:50:34.368 --> 00:50:38.159
Buck spent many hours sitting by the fire and dreaming.

00:50:38.219 --> 00:50:42.410
Sometimes during the day he heard a call from the forest.

00:50:42.471 --> 00:50:46.012
He listened and ran off into the forest.

00:50:46.072 --> 00:50:50.104
He loved running under the tall trees and looking at the birds.

00:50:50.164 --> 00:50:52.754
One night he woke up suddenly.

00:50:52.814 --> 00:50:54.664
He heard the call again.

00:50:54.725 --> 00:50:58.798
It came from the forest and it was a long howl.

00:50:58.858 --> 00:51:02.593
He ran into the forest and followed the sound.

00:51:02.653 --> 00:51:07.467
He came to an open space in the trees and saw a wolf.

00:51:07.528 --> 00:51:11.152
He was sitting and his nose was up in the air.

00:51:11.212 --> 00:51:13.711
He was looking at the sky.

00:51:13.771 --> 00:51:17.530
Buck walked towards him slowly and silently.

00:51:17.590 --> 00:51:21.272
The wolf stopped howling and ran away.

00:51:21.332 --> 00:51:23.193
Buck followed him.

00:51:23.253 --> 00:51:26.895
After some time the wolf stopped and growled at Buck.

00:51:26.955 --> 00:51:29.906
He was afraid because Buck was much bigger.

00:51:29.966 --> 00:51:32.248
But Buck did not want to fight.

00:51:32.308 --> 00:51:34.870
He wanted to make friends with the wolf.

00:51:34.930 --> 00:51:39.130
The wolf understood and they touched noses.

00:51:39.190 --> 00:51:41.758
They became friends and played together.

00:51:41.818 --> 00:51:45.980
They ran for hours through the forest and under the open sky.

00:51:46.040 --> 00:51:48.402
Old memories came back to Buck.

00:51:48.462 --> 00:51:50.463
He was very happy.

00:51:50.523 --> 00:51:55.295
They stopped by a stream to drink and Buck remembered John Thornton.

00:51:55.356 --> 00:52:00.458
The wolf wanted Buck to follow him, but Buck turned and slowly went back.

00:52:00.518 --> 00:52:02.799
The wolf followed him for a while.

00:52:02.860 --> 00:52:05.761
Then he sat down and howled.

00:52:05.821 --> 00:52:09.373
It was a sad howl.

00:52:09.433 --> 00:52:13.795
Thornton was eating dinner when Buck returned.

00:52:13.855 --> 00:52:16.856
He jumped all over Thornton and licked his face.

00:52:16.916 --> 00:52:20.688
For two days and nights, Buck never left Camp.

00:52:20.748 --> 00:52:25.030
He followed Thornton everywhere, but soon Buck heard the call again.

00:52:25.050 --> 00:52:28.752
He thought about his wild brother in the forest.

00:52:28.812 --> 00:52:31.192
Buck began to sleep out at night.

00:52:31.252 --> 00:52:34.384
He stayed away from Camp for three or four days.

00:52:34.444 --> 00:52:36.726
Once he stayed away for a week.

00:52:36.786 --> 00:52:40.580
He looked for his wild brother but could not find him.

00:52:40.640 --> 00:52:44.822
He fished in the streams and killed animals for food.

00:52:44.882 --> 00:52:48.593
Every part of his body was alive and healthy.

00:52:48.653 --> 00:52:52.004
He was stronger and faster than other dogs.

00:52:52.064 --> 00:52:55.296
There was so much energy in Buck.

00:52:55.356 --> 00:53:01.599
One day Buck was going to the forest and Thornton said, What a fantastic dog.

00:53:01.659 --> 00:53:05.717
Hans and Pete agreed.

00:53:05.778 --> 00:53:14.997
Chapter 9 The Call of the Wild In the fall, many moose came to the valley because it was warmer.

00:53:15.057 --> 00:53:17.458
Buck wanted to hunt a big moose.

00:53:17.518 --> 00:53:21.979
The biggest moose was six feet tall and had enormous antlers.

00:53:22.039 --> 00:53:24.650
He was much bigger and stronger than Buck.

00:53:24.710 --> 00:53:28.111
When he saw Buck, he growled angrily.

00:53:28.171 --> 00:53:30.451
Buck followed the moose for many hours.

00:53:30.471 --> 00:53:36.270
He was clever and thought, I must separate him from his group.

00:53:36.330 --> 00:53:41.531
It was not easy, but by evening the moose was away from his group.

00:53:41.591 --> 00:53:43.842
Buck started to attack him.

00:53:43.902 --> 00:53:46.164
Wild animals are patient.

00:53:46.224 --> 00:53:47.865
They do not hurry.

00:53:47.925 --> 00:53:52.438
They wait for the right moment, and then they attack.

00:53:52.498 --> 00:53:54.670
Buck knew how to wait.

00:53:54.730 --> 00:53:58.863
For four days Buck attacked and jumped away.

00:53:58.923 --> 00:54:01.475
Then he danced in front of the big moose.

00:54:01.535 --> 00:54:03.536
He never left him alone.

00:54:03.596 --> 00:54:07.319
The moose could not eat, drink, sleep or rest.

00:54:07.379 --> 00:54:15.674
He became very tired and very weak and stopped for long periods, so Buck ate, drank and rested.

00:54:15.734 --> 00:54:20.788
At the end of the fourth day Buck killed the big moose.

00:54:20.848 --> 00:54:27.569
For a day and a night, he stayed by the dead moose, and ate and slept.

00:54:27.629 --> 00:54:33.310
When he was rested and strong, he decided to return to John Thornton.

00:54:33.370 --> 00:54:39.922
When Buck was five miles from camp, he smelled something strange, something terrible.

00:54:39.982 --> 00:54:41.972
He started running fast.

00:54:42.032 --> 00:54:43.802
The forest was silent.

00:54:43.862 --> 00:54:46.863
There were no birds and no small animals.

00:54:46.923 --> 00:54:50.874
Near some trees, he found the dead body of nigg.

00:54:50.935 --> 00:54:53.366
He had an arrow in his body.

00:54:53.426 --> 00:54:57.078
He found another sled dog with an arrow in his neck.

00:54:57.138 --> 00:55:00.981
Near the camp, Buck heard voices singing.

00:55:01.041 --> 00:55:05.704
Then he found Han's body with arrows in his back.

00:55:05.764 --> 00:55:09.796
A wild, terrible anger grew in Buck.

00:55:09.856 --> 00:55:12.328
He could not control his anger.

00:55:12.388 --> 00:55:18.512
He saw the Yehat Indians dancing at Thornton's camp and he suddenly attacked them.

00:55:18.572 --> 00:55:20.653
He wanted to destroy them.

00:55:20.713 --> 00:55:22.824
Buck was faster than the wind.

00:55:22.884 --> 00:55:26.537
He jumped at the Indians with all his strength and anger.

00:55:26.597 --> 00:55:29.939
He cut the throat of two Indians with his sharp teeth.

00:55:29.999 --> 00:55:33.601
Nothing could stop him and he killed many Yehats.

00:55:33.661 --> 00:55:35.232
He was like a devil.

00:55:35.292 --> 00:55:39.535
The Indians escaped into the forest but Buck followed them.

00:55:39.595 --> 00:55:43.906
When Buck returned to the camp, he found Pete's body.

00:55:43.966 --> 00:55:47.047
He followed Thornton's smell to a pool.

00:55:47.107 --> 00:55:50.558
Buck knew Thornton's body was in the pool.

00:55:50.618 --> 00:55:53.458
He stayed by the pool all day.

00:55:53.518 --> 00:55:56.319
He knew John Thornton was dead.

00:55:56.379 --> 00:56:00.550
Now, he was very sad and alone.

00:56:00.610 --> 00:56:05.811
When he looked at the dead Yihats, he was proud of himself.

00:56:05.871 --> 00:56:08.682
That night there was a full moon.

00:56:08.742 --> 00:56:11.724
Buck heard the sounds of the forest.

00:56:11.784 --> 00:56:14.014
They became louder.

00:56:14.074 --> 00:56:19.105
It was the call of the wild, and he was ready to obey.

00:56:19.165 --> 00:56:21.686
John Thornton was dead.

00:56:21.746 --> 00:56:23.826
He was completely free.

00:56:23.846 --> 00:56:27.347
A wolf pack entered Buck's valley.

00:56:27.407 --> 00:56:30.057
He watched them silently.

00:56:30.117 --> 00:56:33.684
They were afraid because Buck was so big.

00:56:33.744 --> 00:56:38.532
But then one wolf jumped at Buck, and he attacked and broke the wolf's neck.

00:56:38.592 --> 00:56:41.994
Three other wolves jumped at him, but he attacked them.

00:56:42.054 --> 00:56:45.326
Finally, all the wolf pack attacked Buck.

00:56:45.386 --> 00:56:48.658
He jumped at them with his great strength and intelligence.

00:56:48.718 --> 00:56:50.410
They could not stop him.

00:56:50.470 --> 00:56:53.502
After half an hour, the pack went away.

00:56:53.562 --> 00:56:55.273
They were very tired.

00:56:55.333 --> 00:56:58.696
One wolf was friendly and went close to Buck.

00:56:58.756 --> 00:57:00.676
Buck remembered him.

00:57:00.736 --> 00:57:03.042
It was his wild brother.

00:57:03.102 --> 00:57:05.486
They touched noses.

00:57:05.546 --> 00:57:08.158
Other wolves came to make friends.

00:57:08.218 --> 00:57:13.330
An old wolf sat down, looked at the moon and howled.

00:57:13.390 --> 00:57:16.391
The other sat down and howled too.

00:57:16.451 --> 00:57:19.132
Buck did the same.

00:57:19.192 --> 00:57:23.664
Soon the wolves were all around Buck and smelled him.

00:57:23.724 --> 00:57:27.626
Then they ran into the forest and Buck ran with them.

00:57:27.686 --> 00:57:30.546
His wild brother ran by his side.

00:57:30.607 --> 00:57:41.989
Perhaps this is the end of Buck's story, but after a few years, the Yehat Indians saw that some wolves had brown in their gray coats.

00:57:42.050 --> 00:57:47.461
They also saw a ghost dog at the front of the wolf pack.

00:57:47.521 --> 00:57:52.962
When the Yehats follow the moose, they do not enter a certain valley.

00:57:53.022 --> 00:58:00.482
In the summer, there is a visitor in that valley, a big golden brown wolf.

00:58:00.542 --> 00:58:03.530
He is bigger than any other wolf.

00:58:03.590 --> 00:58:10.284
He goes to a yellow stream, stops there, and then howls.

00:58:10.344 --> 00:58:13.196
But he is not always alone.

00:58:13.256 --> 00:58:16.097
He is the leader of the wolf pack.

00:58:16.157 --> 00:58:22.201
He runs in the moonlight and sings the song of the pack.

00:58:22.261 --> 00:58:24.732
Exercise 2.

00:58:24.792 --> 00:58:28.686
Listening Why are you afraid of the valley?

00:58:28.746 --> 00:58:33.038
We are afraid of that valley, because a ghost dog lives there.

00:58:33.098 --> 00:58:34.378
A ghost dog?

00:58:34.438 --> 00:58:35.449
Yes.

00:58:35.509 --> 00:58:39.140
A big brown dog with long white fangs.

00:58:39.201 --> 00:58:41.371
He is bigger than a wolf.

00:58:41.432 --> 00:58:43.432
He growls at people.

00:58:43.493 --> 00:58:48.514
In the summer, he sits near a yellow stream and looks at the water.

00:58:48.574 --> 00:58:50.596
Sometimes he cries.

00:58:50.656 --> 00:58:54.357
At night, he looks at the stars and howls.

00:58:54.417 --> 00:58:56.390
Is he always alone?

00:58:56.450 --> 00:58:59.772
No, he is the leader of a wolf pack.

00:58:59.832 --> 00:59:03.694
He runs in the valley, and the wolves follow him.

00:59:03.754 --> 00:59:06.274
Is there any gold in the yellow stream?

00:59:06.334 --> 00:59:08.876
Yes, there is lots of gold.

00:59:08.936 --> 00:59:11.606
But everyone is afraid to enter the valley.

00:59:11.667 --> 00:59:13.877
Do you hunt the moose in the valley?

00:59:13.937 --> 00:59:15.758
No, never.

00:59:15.818 --> 00:59:22.204
The ghost dog is very dangerous.

00:59:22.264 --> 00:59:26.019
you

